WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:03.483
True position, part three. Into three D,

2
00:00:03.583 --> 00:00:06.325
where the tolerance zone becomes a cylinder.

3
00:00:09.033 --> 00:00:10.473
In part one we drew the zone as

4
00:00:10.573 --> 00:00:12.708
a circle, looking straight down on the plate.

5
00:00:12.800 --> 00:00:15.813
But a hole has depth. Tip the part over, and you'll

6
00:00:15.913 --> 00:00:18.682
see the circle is really the end of a cylinder.

7
00:00:18.766 --> 00:00:21.191
The zone extends through the full depth of the

8
00:00:21.291 --> 00:00:23.277
hole, and it stands square to datum A.

9
00:00:23.866 --> 00:00:26.436
To find the axis, the C M M probes the hole wall

10
00:00:26.536 --> 00:00:29.828
at several depths, at least near the top and near the bottom.

11
00:00:29.916 --> 00:00:31.844
The axis that counts is the axis of the

12
00:00:31.944 --> 00:00:34.495
largest perfect pin that would fit inside the hole.

13
00:00:34.595 --> 00:00:37.354
The standard calls that pin the actual mating envelope.

14
00:00:38.550 --> 00:00:42.124
Here's the zone cylinder, magnified sideways so we can see

15
00:00:42.224 --> 00:00:45.291
inside. The yellow line is the true position axis.

16
00:00:45.383 --> 00:00:48.393
A straight hole that's square to A, but shifted a

17
00:00:48.493 --> 00:00:51.186
little, has the same error at the top and at

18
00:00:51.286 --> 00:00:55.122
the bottom. Position is forty-five ten-thousandths. It passes.

19
00:00:55.216 --> 00:00:58.342
Now the drill wanders. The top of the hole is still

20
00:00:58.442 --> 00:01:01.505
in the same place, but the bottom has drifted out.

21
00:01:01.600 --> 00:01:05.644
Check each end. The top is still forty-five ten-thousandths.

22
00:01:05.744 --> 00:01:08.408
At the bottom, delta X is four and delta

23
00:01:08.508 --> 00:01:12.622
Y is five thousandths: that's twelve point eight thousandths.

24
00:01:12.722 --> 00:01:15.937
The axis leaves the cylinder, so the hole fails.

25
00:01:16.033 --> 00:01:19.872
Looking only at the top of the hole, this part would have passed. The

26
00:01:19.972 --> 00:01:23.810
whole depth has to be in the zone, so position reports the worst end.

27
00:01:23.910 --> 00:01:27.292
Most C M M software checks the axis at both ends of the hole.

28
00:01:28.483 --> 00:01:31.369
Because the zone is a cylinder square to A, it limits

29
00:01:31.469 --> 00:01:34.469
tilt too. The most tilt that can still pass runs corner

30
00:01:34.569 --> 00:01:37.512
to corner: ten thousandths over the depth of the hole.

31
00:01:37.600 --> 00:01:40.479
If the hole needs to be straighter than that, the designer

32
00:01:40.579 --> 00:01:43.869
can add a perpendicularity callout under it. That zone is smaller,

33
00:01:43.969 --> 00:01:46.489
and it can float anywhere inside the position zone.

34
00:01:46.583 --> 00:01:49.855
The tighter perpendicularity controls tilt.

35
00:01:49.955 --> 00:01:52.442
Position still controls location.

36
00:01:53.633 --> 00:01:57.186
The diameter symbol decides the shape of the zone. With it,

37
00:01:57.286 --> 00:01:59.910
the zone is a cylinder, for a hole or a pin.

38
00:02:00.000 --> 00:02:03.426
Without it, the zone is two parallel planes. That's used for

39
00:02:03.526 --> 00:02:06.601
a slot or a tab, where only one direction matters: the

40
00:02:06.701 --> 00:02:09.481
center plane of the slot has to lie between them.

41
00:02:09.566 --> 00:02:13.169
Watch for that symbol when you read the frame. Without the diameter,

42
00:02:13.269 --> 00:02:16.491
the ten thousandths is a total width, so the center plane can

43
00:02:16.591 --> 00:02:19.977
be off at most five thousandths to either side of true position.

44
00:02:21.166 --> 00:02:24.732
Position also controls coaxial features, like a turned diameter

45
00:02:24.832 --> 00:02:26.826
that has to run true to another one.

46
00:02:26.916 --> 00:02:30.456
Datum A is the axis of the large diameter. The small

47
00:02:30.556 --> 00:02:34.587
diameter's axis must lie in a cylinder around datum axis A.

48
00:02:34.683 --> 00:02:37.790
This matters more under the two thousand eighteen

49
00:02:37.890 --> 00:02:42.174
standard. It removed the concentricity symbol completely. Position,

50
00:02:42.274 --> 00:02:45.316
runout or profile are used instead. You'll still

51
00:02:45.416 --> 00:02:48.719
see concentricity on older two thousand nine prints.

52
00:02:49.416 --> 00:02:52.833
Next, in part four: material modifiers. M M

53
00:02:52.933 --> 00:02:55.287
C, L M C, and bonus tolerance.
